# THE TUNING (v0.3, Setup 2 KNOB 4, par110): a pitch knob's detent is the grid's next step, up or down (Evan,
# 2026-10-30, after #61's glide-and-land: every detent moves the pitch, and the card shows the note it goes to).
# Drone I's pitch (par0, cents over MIDI 0; D3 5000); the host's spin turns its detents at once: a first turn, no
# speed-up
set 74 0
set 51 0
tap PLAY
wait 500
expect par110 0
expect par0 5000
# four detents: four semitones, at once (F#3)
page 1
spin K1 4
page 0
expect par0 5400
wait 900
expect par0 5400
# SEL fine-tunes, 1 cent a detent, and that stays: +3 over every semitone it steps to after
press SEL
page 1
spin K1 3
page 0
release SEL
expect par0 5403
page 1
spin K1 2
page 0
expect par0 5603
page 1
spin K1 -1
page 0
expect par0 5503
# the grid goes round both ways: quarter tones (1)
tap GLO
tap GLO
spin K1 -1
expect par110 10
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
expect par110 1
# ... a detent is a quarter tone, and the new Tuning let SEL's +3 go (Evan, 2026-11-07): from 5503 to the next
# quarter tone, 5550
tap HOME
page 1
spin K1 1
page 0
expect par0 5550
# just intonation (5, Ptolemy's, movable: built on drone I, Evan 2026-10-30): drone I's knob picks the tonic in
# semitones, from 5550 (off the semitones) down four: 5500 5400 5300 5200
tap GLO
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
expect par110 5
tap HOME
page 1
spin K1 -4
page 0
expect par0 5200
# ... and drone II's (par21, 5700: 500 over drone I) steps through the just intervals over it: up to 45/32 (5790),
# down to 4/3, 5/4 (5698, 5586)
expect par21 5700
page 1
spin K3 1
page 0
expect par21 5790
page 1
spin K3 -2
page 0
expect par21 5586
# 53-tone (4): 1200/53 = 22.6 cents a step, from A (900): 5200 is 4300 over A, under step 190 (4302); two up, 190
# and 191: 5225
tap GLO
spin K1 -1
expect par110 4
tap HOME
page 1
spin K1 2
page 0
expect par0 5225
# the Tunings in order (40: simplest to richest): 5 Just, 6 Harmonics, 7 LMY, 8 Harrison, 9 Shruti, 10 Partch
# LMY (7): La Monte Young's Well-Tuned Piano, as Ableton's file places it (A 440 one of its notes): uneven steps,
# one each detent. E4+2 (6402, 3/2 over A3) up: 6429 (32/21), 6465 (14/9), 6669 (7/4); down again: 6465 6429 6402
tap GLO
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
expect par110 7
tap HOME
set 0 6402
page 1
spin K1 1
page 0
expect par0 6429
page 1
spin K1 1
page 0
expect par0 6465
page 1
spin K1 1
page 0
expect par0 6669
page 1
spin K1 -1
page 0
expect par0 6465
page 1
spin K1 -1
page 0
expect par0 6429
page 1
spin K1 -1
page 0
expect par0 6402
wait 900
expect par0 6402
# the harmonics (6): from 6402 (702 over A3, the 3rd harmonic) up: 841 (13th): 6541
tap GLO
spin K1 -1
expect par110 6
tap HOME
page 1
spin K1 1
page 0
expect par0 6541
# the shrutis (9, movable as Just: Sa on drone I): drone I's knob in semitones, 6541 up: 6600; drone II's (5586,
# 1014 under drone I: 186 over Sa an octave down, by 10/9's 182) up to 9/8: 5604
tap GLO
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
expect par110 9
tap HOME
page 1
spin K1 1
page 0
expect par0 6600
page 1
spin K3 1
page 0
expect par21 5604
# Lou Harrison's (8, his National Steel guitar's, A 440 one of its notes): 6600 (900 over A3, over 5/3's 884) up:
# 996 (16/9): 6696;
# down twice: 6584, 6465 (14/9)
tap GLO
spin K1 -1
expect par110 8
tap HOME
page 1
spin K1 1
page 0
expect par0 6696
page 1
spin K1 -2
page 0
expect par0 6465
# Harry Partch's 43 (10), from A: 6465 (765 over A3, 14/9) up: 792, 814 (128/81, 8/5): 6514
tap GLO
spin K1 1
spin K1 1
expect par110 10
tap HOME
page 1
spin K1 2
page 0
expect par0 6514
tap GLO
spin K1 1
expect par110 0
spin K1 -1
expect par110 10
spin K1 1
tap HOME
# Pitch link on (par45): drone II's knob turns the link offset (par46), a step of the grid's intervals: a fifth
# (700) up one: 800
set 45 1
set 46 700
page 1
spin K3 1
page 0
expect par46 800
# A SOUND CARRIES ITS TUNING (ledger 3, Evan 2026-11-08): a scene stored on 19-tone brings 19-tone back, and lets go
# of SEL's fine tuning as it does; a Preset that names none is 12-tone, as it was made, Pitch lock on or off; the
# Tuning flips half way through the scene's glide, never through the ones between
set 45 0
set 71 24
tap GLO
tap GLO
set 110 2
expect par110 2
tap HOME
press SEL
tapkey w8
release SEL
press SAVE
tapkey w0
release SAVE
wait 300
set 110 7
press SEL
page 1
spin K1 3
page 0
release SEL
expect tunoff0 >0
tapkey w0
wait 300
expect par110 7
wait 1200
expect par110 2
expect tunoff0 0
# the Presets (SEL + F5), Pitch lock on: P1 Niagara names no Tuning, so 12-tone
set 74 1
press SEL
tapkey w14
release SEL
tapkey w0
wait 1500
expect par110 0
# SEL's fine tuning comes back with its Tuning when a blend does (the review of #82): drone I on D3 (on 12-tone's
# notes) +3; A1 (19-tone) pressed in past half way lets it go; let go, the sound goes back: 12-tone and +3 return;
# tapped, then SEL + SAVE (undo): the same
set 74 0
press SEL
tapkey w8
release SEL
set 0 5000
wait 300
press SEL
page 1
spin K1 3
page 0
release SEL
expect par110 0
expect tunoff0 3
key w0 down
pressure w0 127
wait 1800
expect par110 2
expect tunoff0 0
pressure w0 0
key w0 up
wait 1800
expect par110 0
expect tunoff0 3
tapkey w0
wait 1500
expect par110 2
expect tunoff0 0
press SEL
tap SAVE
release SEL
wait 1500
expect par110 0
expect tunoff0 3
